"""Policy / evidence templates auditors ask for (starting points - adapt, review with legal/compliance advisers)."""
HEAD = "> **Template - not legal advice.** Adapt to your organization, have it approved by management and review it at least yearly.\n\n"
P = {
"01-information-security-policy.md": "# Information Security Policy\n\n**Owner:** _role_  ·  **Approved by:** _name, date_  ·  **Review:** annually\n\n## Purpose & scope\nProtect the confidentiality, integrity and availability of company and customer data across all systems, people and vendors.\n\n## Principles\n- Least privilege and need-to-know; MFA for all production, cloud, code and admin access.\n- Secure by default: encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest; secrets only in a secret manager.\n- Changes go through version control, review and automated tests; no direct production edits.\n- Security events are logged, monitored and investigated.\n\n## Responsibilities\n| Role | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| Management | Sets risk appetite, funds controls |\n| Engineering | Secure development, patching, access reviews |\n| Everyone | Report incidents immediately, complete annual training |\n\n## Exceptions\nDocumented, time-boxed, approved by _role_.\n",
"02-access-control-policy.md": "# Access Control Policy\n\n- Accounts are individual; no shared credentials. SSO + MFA wherever supported.\n- Access is granted by role, approved by the manager, logged in a ticket; removed within **24 h** of leaving/role change.\n- **Quarterly access review** of cloud, source control, database, CI/CD and SaaS admins; evidence stored (date, reviewer, changes).\n- Privileged access is time-boxed and audited; production data access requires business justification.\n- Passwords: password manager, ≥ 14 chars or passkeys; service credentials rotated ≥ yearly and on suspicion.\n",
"03-secure-development-policy.md": "# Secure Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) Policy\n\n1. All code in Git; protected `main`; pull requests require review.\n2. CI on every PR: lint, type-check, tests, dependency audit, secret scan, SAST (e.g. PN-Ultra-Audit).\n3. Critical/high findings block release unless an approved, dated exception exists; medium within 30 days; low within 90 days.\n4. Dependencies pinned (lockfile) and monitored (Dependabot/Renovate); SBOM generated per release.\n5. Secrets never in code; `.env` ignored; rotate on exposure.\n6. Threat modeling for new features handling sensitive data; security review before launch.\n7. Annual third-party penetration test and remediation tracking.\n",
"04-change-management-policy.md": "# Change Management Policy\n\n- Every production change = a pull request linked to a ticket, reviewed by someone other than the author, and passing CI.\n- Emergency changes allowed with post-hoc review within 2 business days.\n- Releases are tagged, reproducible and reversible (rollback plan documented).\n- Database migrations are versioned, reviewed and tested on a copy of production data.\n- Evidence: PR history, CI logs, release notes.\n",
"05-incident-response-plan.md": "# Incident Response Plan\n\n## Severity\n| Level | Example | Response |\n|---|---|---|\n| SEV1 | Confirmed data breach, outage of core service | Immediate, incident commander, exec notified |\n| SEV2 | Suspected compromise, partial outage | < 1 h |\n| SEV3 | Vulnerability, minor degradation | < 1 business day |\n\n## Phases\n1. **Detect & triage** (alerts, error tracking, reports) 2. **Contain** (revoke keys, isolate systems) 3. **Eradicate & recover** 4. **Notify** (customers/regulators: **GDPR 72 h**, HIPAA breach rule, contracts) 5. **Post-incident review** within 5 days with action items.\n\n## Contacts\nIncident commander: _name_ · Legal/DPO: _name_ · Comms: _name_ · Vendor support lines: _list_\n",
"06-backup-and-disaster-recovery.md": "# Backup & Disaster Recovery Plan\n\n- Databases: automated daily backups, **retention ≥ 30 days**, encrypted, stored in a separate account/region.\n- **Restore test every quarter** (evidence: date, duration, result). Targets: **RPO** _x h_, **RTO** _y h_.\n- Infrastructure as code so environments can be rebuilt; secrets recoverable from the secret manager.\n- Annual DR exercise with lessons learned.\n",
"07-data-retention-and-privacy.md": "# Data Classification, Retention & Privacy\n\n| Class | Examples | Controls |\n|---|---|---|\n| Restricted | credentials, health/financial data, keys | encryption, strict access, audit log |\n| Confidential | customer data, source code | role-based access |\n| Internal / Public | docs / marketing | standard |\n\n- **Records of Processing (GDPR Art. 30)**: purpose, categories, recipients, transfers, retention, security measures (see ropa-template).\n- Retention: delete or anonymize data when no longer needed; honor access/erasure requests within **30 days**.\n- Cookie/tracking consent before non-essential tags (ePrivacy/GDPR); consent log kept.\n- Data Processing Agreements with every processor; transfer mechanism (SCCs) for non-EEA transfers.\n",
"08-vendor-management-policy.md": "# Vendor / Third-Party Risk Policy\n\n- Maintain a vendor inventory (service, data shared, criticality, owner, contract, DPA, certifications).\n- Before onboarding: security questionnaire or SOC 2 / ISO 27001 report review; define exit plan for critical vendors (DORA).\n- Review critical vendors annually; monitor incidents and sub-processors.\n",
"09-acceptable-use-and-training.md": "# Acceptable Use & Security Awareness\n\n- Company devices: disk encryption, screen lock, auto-updates, endpoint protection (MDM evidence).\n- No personal data or secrets in chat/AI tools unless approved; use approved AI assistants with data controls.\n- Annual security & privacy training + phishing exercise; new-hire training within 30 days (track completion).\n",
"10-risk-assessment-register.md": "# Risk Assessment & Register\n\nPerform annually and after major changes. Score = likelihood (1-5) × impact (1-5).\n\n| ID | Risk | Asset | L | I | Score | Treatment (mitigate/accept/transfer/avoid) | Owner | Due | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R-001 | _e.g. leaked API key in repo_ | source control | 3 | 5 | 15 | Rotate, secret scanning | _name_ | _date_ | open |\n\nInput: PN-Ultra-Audit findings (critical/high), pen-test reports, incidents, vendor reviews.\n",
"ropa-template.md": "# Record of Processing Activities (GDPR Art. 30)\n\n| Processing activity | Purpose & legal basis | Data subjects | Data categories | Recipients / processors | Third-country transfers | Retention | Security measures |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| _e.g. user accounts_ | contract | customers | name, email, hashed password | hosting, email provider | none / SCCs | account life + 12 m | TLS, argon2, RBAC, backups |\n",
}
def all_templates(): return {k: HEAD + v for k, v in P.items()}
